    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1581">

                <pb facs="1275" n="1159" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.00/429.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs replied to request of committee relative to arms
                    reported in my July 9, that arms could be deposited only under guard of the
                    police themselves. Committee has informed him that it could not agree to this
                    interpretation of its authority and duties under President of Panama decree
                    approving instructions to supervisors, and would proceed to comply with these
                    duties, notifying supervisors fully to assert their proper authority.</p>
                <p>Unión Patriótica having requested committee to examine evidence of electoral
                    frauds and put off election until August 11, committee consented to former
                    request, but stated that no proper ground had been shown to consent to latter.
                    Unión Patriótica yesterday published manifesto that Diaz withdrew, and advising
                    their friends not to vote on account of electoral frauds rendering such voting
                    useless.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
